nvme-stas (3.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Non-backward-compatible release. See NEWS.md for the full list.
  * Requires libnvme 3.0 and nvme-cli 3.0. libnvme 3.0 makes significant API
    changes and drops compatibility with prior versions; the Python bindings
    are now the libnvme3 package.
  * All configuration moved to /etc/nvme. /etc/stas is gone, and so are
    sys.conf and the stasadm tool; the host identity now comes from
    /etc/nvme/hostnqn and /etc/nvme/hostid.
  * Which controllers to connect to, and with what parameters, moved out of
    stafd.conf/stacd.conf into /etc/nvme/nvme-stas.conf, in libnvme's INI
    format, read by libnvme's own parser. The controller= keyword and the
    [Global] connection tunables are gone from the daemon configuration files.
  * nvme-stas no longer disconnects connections it did not make: libnvme's
    ownership registry is consulted before adopting one. disconnect-scope and
    disconnect-trtypes are replaced by honor-fabric-zoning. The override that
    suppressed nvme-cli's udev rule is gone.
  * libnvme's host-wide exclusion list (nvme exclusion) is honored; the
    exclude= keyword is deprecated.
  * Discovery connections are held open only where EPCSD says to; a controller
    that cannot hold one is polled instead. persistent-connections is gone and
    zeroconf-connections-persistence is renamed dc-giveup-timeout.
  * Time spans are parsed the way systemd parses them.
  * Renames: dhchap to kxchap (TP4201), host-nqn to hostnqn. The D-Bus data
    format is not compatible with 2.x.

 -- Martin Belanger <martin.belanger@dell.com>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 11:30:00 -0500

